          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p22-q30-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "Evaluate $ffff(x)$ for $x=0$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0$.",
              "worked": "Reading successive outputs from the graph gives $0\\mapsto3\\mapsto0\\mapsto3\\mapsto0$. Thus $f(f(f(f(0))))=0$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          },
          {
            "id": "p22-q30-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "Evaluate $ffff(x)$ for $x=3$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$3$.",
              "worked": "Reading successive outputs from the graph gives $3\\mapsto0\\mapsto3\\mapsto0\\mapsto3$. Thus $f(f(f(f(3))))=3$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          },
          {
            "id": "p22-q30-b-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "Explain geometrically why the pair $\\{0,3\\}$ forms an alternating cycle under composition by $f$, and state other alternating cycles for $f$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "The points $(0,3)$ and $(3,0)$ are reflections in $y=x$, so $f(0)=3$ and $f(3)=0$. Other cycles are $\\{1,2\\}$ and $\\{0.5,2.5\\}$. In general, the distinct two-cycles are $\\{a,3-a\\}$ for $0\\leq a<1.5$; $1.5$ is a fixed point.",
              "worked": "An alternating cycle between distinct values $a$ and $b$ requires $f(a)=b$ and $f(b)=a$. Thus both $(a,b)$ and $(b,a)$ lie on the graph, and these points are mirror reflections in $y=x$.\n\nThe graph contains $(0,3)$ and $(3,0)$, so repeated composition alternates between $0$ and $3$. The segment $y=3-x$ for $0\\leq x\\leq3$ is symmetric in $y=x$. Its reflected point pairs give cycles such as $\\{1,2\\}$ and $\\{0.5,2.5\\}$. All distinct two-cycles can be written as $\\{a,3-a\\}$ with $0\\leq a<1.5$. At $a=1.5$, the two values coincide: $f(1.5)=1.5$, so this is a fixed point rather than an alternating two-cycle.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 42
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
